WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.476
A few numbers capture the impact.

00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:09.032
The lower bound gives a zero-one error of at least
square-root OPT over sixty pi for the logistic minimizer,

00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:13.587
valid whenever OPT is at most one one-hundredth.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:18.143
Under radial Lipschitzness, logistic regression
reaches near-optimal order-OPT error.

00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:22.699
The two-phase algorithm achieves order OPT plus
epsilon error for bounded distributions

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:27.255
and order OPT times log one over OPT for
sub-exponential ones.

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:31.811
It does so with a sample complexity of order d over
epsilon squared,

00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:36.367
a quadratic improvement over the d over epsilon to
the fourth required by prior nonconvex methods.

00:00:36.447 --> 00:00:40.922
And structurally,

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:45.478
whereas earlier algorithms that hit order OPT error
had to solve a logarithmic number

00:00:45.558 --> 00:00:50.034
of minimization problems while guessing OPT by
binary search,

00:00:50.114 --> 00:00:54.590
this method needs only two convex steps.
